[[Has confidence score::0.65]]
[[Has evidence count::12]]
[[Has replication status::Consistent]]
[[Has review type::Meta-analysis]]
```
* Banner: Blue (#BBDEFB)
* Icon: Established building
* Text: "This claim is well-supported by multiple independent sources."


'''Upgrade Criteria:'''
* Widespread acceptance across field
* Textbook inclusion
* No significant scientific controversy
* Predictive success


'''Downgrade Triggers:'''
* Paradigm shift in field


'''Sources:'''
* Goyal, M., et al. (2014). Meditation programs for psychological stress and well-being: A systematic review and meta-analysis. JAMA Internal Medicine, 174(3), 357-368.
* IPCC. (2021). Climate Change 2021: The Physical Science Basis. Cambridge University Press.


=== 2.4 Tier 4: Verified ===


'''Definition:''' Reproducible, independently validated, widely accepted, practically demonstrated.
* Confidence Range: 0.75-0.95
* Evidence Requirement: Reproducibility by independent researchers, textbook inclusion, practical applications
* Validation: Extensive replication and application


'''Examples:'''
* "General relativity accurately predicts gravitational lensing" (verified by 10,000+ observations)
* "Vaccines prevent infectious disease" (verified by billions of administrations)
* "Natural selection drives evolution" (verified across biology)
* "DNA polymerase replicates genetic material" (verified in millions of experiments)
* Foundational knowledge
* Engineering applications
* Educational standards
* Policy foundations
* Absolute certainty (0.95, not 1.0)
* Dismissing all edge cases
* Ignoring scope limitations


